  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "If the external reversal was primarily a stateful-Adam/finite-step boundary effect, actor-only interpolation from matched control toward the alpha=1 MGDA endpoint will reveal a lower nonzero dose with reduced greedy disagreement and no consistent negative fresh payoff slope; monotone negative payoff across doses instead rejects this realized direction.",
  "material_change": "Construct optimizer-free actor-only interpolations at alpha 0.125, 0.25, and 0.5 between the frozen matched control and alpha=1 MGDA endpoint, keeping all non-actor tensors from control. First measure direct output drift, then evaluate geometric doses on one shared untouched common-deck multi-anchor cohort.",
  "baseline": "Alpha=1 online MGDA versus control: actor parameter-step ratio 1.2525, cosine 0.5439, output mean TV 0.006964, greedy disagreement 0.725%, and fresh pooled -5.8441 +/-4.6987 bb/100 with CI upper -1.1454.",
  "source": "Hash-bound control 43e81546b68f1c8f7b0353e6f7dfbcc7aa48853316db3ccd930cd9ddc554d251 and MGDA treatment 2dc0e9e84d2a0e7ab91bc6a8ca7170caa4403d9b9f1d73e8784fa6d6d97744a2; no optimizer continuation is permitted from interpolated artifacts.",
